#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Online services for the station's Online page, saved so the last answer
still shows when the station is offline.

  emcomm-online refresh [--force] [SOURCE...]  fetch alerts, space, bands, heard, alertmap
                                               (default: alerts space bands alertmap)
  emcomm-online lookup CALL                    callsign lookup (QRZ, else HamQTH) and the
                                               station's last aprs.fi position, as JSON

Each source is saved to ~/.cache/emcomm/online/SOURCE.json as
{"updated": time of the last good fetch, "tried": time of the last try,
 "error": text or null, "data": ...}. A failed fetch keeps the old data.
A source isn't fetched again sooner than its minimum interval, which keeps
within each service's rules (PSKReporter asks for one query per five minutes).

Logins and keys come from ~/.config/emcomm/accounts.json, which the Online
page's Accounts button writes: email, qrz_user, qrz_password, hamqth_user,
hamqth_password, aprsfi_key.
"""

